    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/mob/en-us/job/499757/assistant-director-for-business-services": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Business Services",
      "description": "UCONN - Assistant Director for Business Services UCONN Assistant Director for Business Services Job no: 499757 Position type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Division/Equivalent: President School/Unit: Athletics Department/Office: Athletics Business Categories: Administrative Services Apply now JOB SUMMARY The University of Connecticut is seeking applications for the full-time position of Assistant Director for Business Services (Administrative Program Support 2). DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Under the general supervision of the Associate Director of Athletics/Business Services, will coordinate and process all business-related aspects of the Division of Athletics, including but not limited to: Serve as daily liaison to Athletics’ on-site travel agents (currently Anthony Travel), University Travel, and the Accounts Payable/Travel Department. Serve as daily processor for travel card program, including issuance of student-athlete per diem, team travel cash advances, and recruiting host money. Assist staff and coaches in University travel card training. Provide oversight and assistance for reconcilement of team travel expenses, recruiting, and official visit expenses for all sports. Oversee check deposits for the Division of Athletics. Collaborate with Athletic Business Office personnel on the creation, implementation, and communication of internal travel policies and procedures. Other duties as assigned MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. 2 years of experience in an NCAA Division I collegiate athletic department. Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with different departments. Possess a strong work ethic and customer service skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Familiarity with business management software (Jaggaer, Peoplesoft, Felix, Kuali, Concur, etc.). More than 2 years of experience in an NCAA Division I collegiate athletic department, with a focus on group/team travel and individual travel. Knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations. Experience in drafting and implementing internal policies and procedures. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position.  The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits, including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment.  For additional information regarding benefits, please visit UConn Health Benefits and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499757 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on September 15, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and